.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH maw-rollback 1  "maw-rollback " 
.SH NAME
maw\-rollback \- restore a generation\*(Aqs repo and package versions, as a new generation
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmaw rollback\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIGENERATION\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
restore a generation\*(Aqs repo and package versions, as a new generation
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
print what would change without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIGENERATION\fR]
the generation number from `maw generations`; the one before the latest if left out
.SH EXTRA
see: maw help rolling back
